   "question": "<p>The cubic equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^3+3x^2-8x+6=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\gamma\"></span>.</p><p>Without solving the equation, find the cubic equation whose roots are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\alpha-1)\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\beta-1)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\gamma-1)\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w^3+pw^2+qw+r=0\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> are integers to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
